# Build and tooling output. Anchored with a leading slash: these are produced at
# the repository root, and an unanchored pattern also hides a file of the same
# name anywhere else in the tree — an archived copy under docs/ would silently
# never be committed.
/main.js
/data.json
/compliance-report.json
/compliance-report.sarif
/sbom.cdx.json
/security-privacy-failure-report.md
/security-privacy-success-report.md

# Local archive of compliance reports pulled down from a CI run. Deliberately not
# tracked: the workflow keeps those artefacts for 7 days on purpose, and a report
# committed here would go stale against the code it describes.
/Git-privacy-security/
